import RequestProject.Wikidata.Diagnostics

/-!
# Provenance slices and temporal snapshots

Two ways of *restricting* a knowledge base:

* by provenance — keep only statements that carry a reference, or only those
  that carry a reference from a source deemed reliable;
* by time — keep only statements whose validity interval contains the instant of
  the snapshot.

Both are instances of the same phenomenon: a slice contains fewer statements, so
it derives fewer facts and inherits validity.  The monotonicity results below
(`subclassOf_mono`, `instanceOf_mono`) are the reason evidence obtained from a
restricted, more trustworthy slice transfers to the full base but not the other
way round.

Monotonicity needs a hypothesis: deleting a *preferred* statement can promote
normal statements into the truthy projection, so it is stated for knowledge bases
all of whose statements have normal rank (`AllNormal`).
-/

